  "notes": [
    "Mappings are export candidates, not evidence of current console support or editability. Reconcile against current platform locale selector before upload.",
    "No binary language declarations or release notes are exported.",
    "storefront-v2 (2026-11-24): each store composes its description from shared blocks. A paragraph is a list of lines, or an object with lines, bullets and an optional when/unless switch; a line is a field ID, a {field, when/unless} reference, or a list of those joined into one line. See translations/README.md.",
    "Switches follow facts/storefront-v2-claims.md. ai_coplay is false for the Mac App Store (R7) and Epic (R8) until each is verified. online_play is false for Microsoft and Epic while their packages are older than 0.11.7.0 (R6); the Amazon edition has no online play, so its composition never references it. Flip a switch only when the claims record changes.",
    "Numbered Microsoft keys (feature_N, search_term_N, desktop_screenshot_caption_N, trailer_title_N) follow tools/microsoft_import.py FIELD_FAMILIES. desktop_screenshot_caption_N must match the final gallery order of the clean desktop screenshot set.",
    "Epic About text is entered as heading and body items; the composed epic description shows their order and content. tools/epic_template.py still maps the storefront-v1 item layout and must be updated before an Epic import.",
    "Snap non-English locale fields remain unverified. Amazon documented supported language labels are exported even while current review prevents saving; exact API codes must be reconciled before use.",
    "2026-11-17 official-documentation review adds supported preparation mappings for the twelve-language expansion: Play 12, Apple 9 per platform, Microsoft 12, Epic 6 and F-Droid 12. Current console/template reconciliation remains required before hosted-store writes; F-Droid source preparation uses documented BCP47 locale directories. See planning/storefront-localization-rollout.md for sources and exact remaining gaps."
  ],
